# What this is: keeps machine-generated state and local secrets out of
# version control starting from this project's very first commit, before any
# tool (including BrotherMode's own store) has had a chance to set up its own
# ignore rules. Who reads this: git, and any human wondering why a file they
# expected to see committed is missing.

# BrotherMode's own local state, if this project uses it. A fresh copy of
# this template has none of these yet; this line stops the very first commit
# from accidentally capturing them once they appear.
.brothermode/
STATE.md
threads/

# Local secrets and environment files. Never commit a real key; if one of
# these already has real content, that content should live in your secret
# manager or your shell environment instead, not in this file's contents.
.env
.env.local
*.pem
*.key

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp
__pycache__/
*.bak*

# Placeholder: add your language or framework's own build output directory
# here once you have chosen one (for example node_modules/, dist/, build/,
# .venv/). Record that choice in decisions/, do not just add the line here
# silently.
